# Only needed when the webapp is deployed on a *different* origin than the server, e.g.
# this webapp on Vercel/Netlify and the server on Render. Leave unset for docker-compose
# (nginx reverse-proxies /api and /socket.io to the server on the same origin) and for local
# dev (vite.config.js already proxies /api and /socket.io to API_URL for you).
#
# This is a Vite build-time variable: it gets baked into the built JS, so set it in the
# hosting platform's build environment (e.g. Vercel project settings) before building, not
# at runtime. Must also be added to the server's ALLOWED_ORIGINS (see server/.env.example).
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-server.onrender.com
